SpectrumAPI module delivery notice

This archive targets arm64-v8a Android 17 / API 37 and requires a separately
installed, enabled Zygisk Next. Only /system/bin/audioserver is declared as
an injection target. Zygisk Next directly loads lib/libspectrum_payload.so
through its FD injection entry; no second library is opened by module path.
This module does not overlay ROM libraries or bundle a root CLI.

Only audioserver process execmem is added to SELinux policy. No broad SELinux
allow rules or automatic restart scripts are included.

lib/libspectrum_payload.so links the Android NDK static C++ runtime
(c++_static) so single-FD injection never opens module-directory shared
libraries from audioserver. Upstream NDK and AOSP source notices are included
under notices/. No ROM library, ROM attachment, official Zygisk Next API
header, or Zygisk Next runtime binary is redistributed in this module.

Build artifact SHA-256 values are provenance/integrity inventory only.
See runtime-boundaries.json and build-info.json for machine-readable details.

The pure-Java SDK connects directly to the native Binder extension on
media.audio_flinger and does not require the optional Manager APK or any UID
grant configuration. Discovery uses ServiceManager.checkService, a non-SDK
entry point which some ROMs may restrict. No hidden-API exemptions, JNI
discovery bridge, alternate backend or automatic reconnect is provided.

The separately distributed Manager APK is an optional modern Xposed/LibXposed
SystemUI media-island display and settings app. Its empty-by-default media
whitelist, actual attached/visible island, local-playing state and full target
APP_UID jointly gate Super Island subscriptions; it never requests ALL_MEDIA
and never invokes su at runtime.
